request.description:
Invoke the `hello` edge function — ai/supabase/volumes/functions/hello/index.ts, a plain Deno.serve handler. Returns { message, method, timestamp }.

This function is OURS, not upstream's sample: upstream's imports @supabase/server and authenticates with the new publishable/secret keys, which 401 in this deployment's legacy HS256 mode.

Errors: 401 when SUPABASE_FUNCTIONS_VERIFY_JWT=true and the Bearer token is missing or invalid (the setting applies to ALL functions — there is no per-function override). 503 while supabase-functions is starting; it waits on the gateway being healthy.

See ai/supabase/SUPABASE.md § Vendored config.

#### Schemas

Unauthenticated while SUPABASE_FUNCTIONS_VERIFY_JWT is false (this deployment's default).

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "$comment": "ours: the whole body",
  "required": ["message", "method", "timestamp"],
  "properties": {
    "message": {"const": "hello from supabase edge functions"},
    "method": {"type": "string", "description": "The request's method"},
    "timestamp": {"type": "string", "description": "UTC ISO 8601 (`toISOString()`)"}
  }
}
```

Response `401` (`application/json`) — only with SUPABASE_FUNCTIONS_VERIFY_JWT=true: no, or a bad, Bearer token (the same code in the `sb-error-code` header):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "$comment": "main/index.ts getAuthErrorResponse",
  "required": ["code", "message", "msg"],
  "properties": {
    "code": {
      "enum": [
        "UNAUTHORIZED_LEGACY_JWT",
        "UNAUTHORIZED_ASYMMETRIC_JWT",
        "UNAUTHORIZED_INVALID_JWT_FORMAT",
        "UNAUTHORIZED_UNSUPPORTED_TOKEN_ALGORITHM",
        "UNAUTHORIZED_NO_AUTH_HEADER"
      ]
    },
    "message": {"type": "string"},
    "msg": {"type": "string", "description": "Deprecated copy of `message`"}
  }
}
```

Realtime tenant health — the same check the container's own healthcheck runs. Returns { data: { healthy, db_connected, connected_cluster } }.

`realtime-dev` is the tenant name Realtime derives from the hostname it is reached at, which is why the Envoy cluster config addresses the container as realtime-dev.supabase-realtime and the compose file adds that as a network alias on supabase_net.

Errors: 401 when the Bearer token was signed with a different SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET. `healthy: false` with `db_connected: false` after a secret rotation is the one-shot-secret trap — Realtime stores the tenant's jwt_secret encrypted under SUPABASE_REALTIME_DB_ENC_KEY. See SUPABASE.md § Secrets that are one-shot.

#### Schemas

`healthy: false, db_connected: false` after a SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET rotation is the one-shot-secret trap (SUPABASE.md § Secrets that are one-shot). 404 for an unknown tenant.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["data"],
  "properties": {
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["healthy", "db_connected", "connected_cluster"],
      "properties": {
        "healthy": {"type": "boolean"},
        "db_connected": {"type": "boolean"},
        "replication_connected": {"type": "boolean"},
        "connected_cluster": {"type": "integer", "description": "Clients connected to the tenant"},
        "region": {"type": ["string", "null"]},
        "node": {"type": "string"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```
